-- title:
--   Action of an end stabiliser on the UV-crossing model
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓ12`, `hℓM'`).
--
--   **Coefficients, level, function field.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), and `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ — with the kernel of the reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. By `hK`, $K$ is the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image, under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), of the rational $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   **Base ring and chart algebra.** $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring which is a domain with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$ (scalar tower), with $q$ in its maximal ideal (`hAq`) and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`); $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal (`hϖ`), and `hϖt` provides $\varpi_t \in A$ and a unit $u$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = qu$. The element $j \in K$ has Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular $j$-invariant (`hj`) and is nonzero. Here `chartAlgFin A K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A K j` $= j$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra for $j$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the chart algebra for $j^{-1}$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with `ιFin` the canonical morphism from `XFin A K j` $= \operatorname{Spec}(\mathtt{chartAlgFin } A\, K\, j)$.
--
--   **Supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of the chart algebra (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0 \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The local Drinfeld-chart hypotheses `hArig` and `hW₁`.** For a point $z$ of the two-chart model at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back through `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and a point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` with `ιFin` $y' = z$ at which the supersingularity condition above holds for $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, the data in question consist of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma\varpi$, power series $f, u, v \in W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]$ with $u, v$ units and $f$ congruent to [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S := W[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu\bigr)$. Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the map from the stalk to its completion, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map onto $S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map from the chart algebra to the stalk at $z$ through the open immersion `ιFin`, seven clauses are required: (i) $e$ carries the image of the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau \in \operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f_0, g_0$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g_0 \ne 0$, and all $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the ratio of those $q$-expansions, the image of $\tau x$ under an embedding $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ equals the ratio of the $q$-expansions of $f_0$ and $g_0$ slashed by the matrix `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` — the automorphism $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$, the restriction of such a $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving the chart algebra and congruent to the identity modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ with the restriction of $\tau$; $\theta$ fixing all classes of constant series; $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}\,\mathrm{mkS}\,X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$; $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod \ell$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$; (v) for integers $a_1,b_1,a_2,b_2$ and primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0$ and $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, each containing $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma\varpi)$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + h_i$ with $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to the stalk along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ are distinct; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above containing $X_0$ up to terms of order two, and for $a$ in the chart algebra, $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ lies in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the series obtained from the $j$-expansion by substituting the $q$-th power of the variable, lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that $\sum_{i \le e_0} \operatorname{coeff}_{(i,\,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{\,e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ not both in the maximal ideal with $a^qb - ab^q$ in the maximal ideal, and $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\,\cdot\, - a_0)))$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` asserts that such data exist at every point $z$ and $y'$ as described. In addition, a specific point $z$ with germ $\varpi z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hϖz`, `hz`), a specific $y'$ above it (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), and specific data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ (`hσ₁`, `hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁`) are fixed, `hW₁` asserting the seven clauses above for these data.
--
--   **The ideal $J$, the ring $B$ and the valuation ring $W$.** By `hJ`, $J$ is the infimum of those ideals of the chart algebra that arise as the contraction, along the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra, of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0$ and $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$, as $\gamma$ ranges over $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving the chart algebra. By `hB`, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ obtained by adjoining to the chart algebra all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$. Furthermore $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` states that the chart algebra is contained in $B$ and that every element of $K$ is a ratio of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; `hR2` states that $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is the image of $A$, that the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of the chart algebra lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at that maximal ideal.
--
--   **The hypothesis `hEQ`** (five clauses) describes the special fibre: (1) for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by $\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}\,q\,k - 1$, whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is $c \in \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\mathtt{redQ } q\, \gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the subgroup of pairs whose determinant times $c^{q+1}$ is $1$, such that $\rho \circ \tau = \mathtt{hAction}\,q\,k\,(\cdot) \circ \rho$ on $B$, and $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (2) $B$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (3) every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ contains the image, under some level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, of all elements of $B$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W$; (4) an element of $B$ all of whose translates by such automorphisms lie in the maximal ideal of $W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; (5) a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserves $y$ on the chart algebra preserves $W$.
--
--   **The stabiliser data.** $n \ge 1$ divides $q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`); $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀q`, `hγ₀M`) and $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (`hτ₀`) preserving $W$ (`hτ₀W`) such that $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B$ pointwise (`hcyc1`) while for each $0 < k < n$ some element of $B$ is moved by $\tau_0^k$ (`hcyc2`). The integer $m \ge 1$ satisfies $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hm1`, `hmt`).
--
--   **The end $O$ and its crossing presentation.** $O$ is a subring of $K$ for which `hO` requires: an element $a \in J$ with nonzero image in $K$ such that, setting $B_a$ to be the $A$-subalgebra generated over the chart algebra by all $x \in K$ with $xa \in J$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (the elements of $K$ of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B_a$, $h \notin P$), every element of $y$ becoming a non-unit in $O$, and $B$ not contained in $O$. Moreover $O$ is stable under $\tau_0$ (`hOτ`), contained in $W$ (`hOW`), local (`hOloc`) and Noetherian (`hOnoe`), and contains the chart algebra (`hCO`). Writing $\hat A$ for the adic completion of $A$ at its maximal ideal and $\hat\varpi$ for the image of $\varpi$, the map $\iota$ is a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A\,(\hat\varpi^{\,m}) = \hat A[\![X_0,X_1]\!]/(X_0X_1 - \hat\varpi^{\,m})$, carrying the class of $a \in A$ (when its image lies in $O$) to `UVCrossingModel.const` of $\hat a$ (`hιc`), and $\varpi$ lies in $O$ (`hϖO`). Finally $c_x, c_y \in O$ and units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of the model satisfy $\iota(\hat c_x) = \gamma_U \cdot U$ and $\iota(\hat c_y) = \gamma_V \cdot V$ (`hιx`, `hιy`), where $U$ and $V$ are the two distinguished elements `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V` of the model; and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W$ whenever it lies in $W$ (`hcyW`), while $c_x$ does not (`hcxW`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism $\theta_0$ of `UVCrossingModel` $\hat A\,(\hat\varpi^{\,m})$ such that:
--
--   1. for every $f \in K$ with $f \in O$ and $\tau_0 f \in O$, the image under $\iota$ of the class of $\tau_0 f$ equals $\theta_0$ applied to the image under $\iota$ of the class of $f$;
--
--   2. $\theta_0(U)$ does not lie in the ideal generated by $V$ and by `UVCrossingModel.const` of $\hat\varpi$;
--
--   3. the $n$-th power of $\theta_0$, taken as a ring isomorphism of the model, acts as the identity on every element.
--
--   This is the end-action step in the local analysis of the supersingular fibre at auxiliary level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ guard prime: the generator $\tau_0$ of the stabiliser of an end of the blow-up acts on the completed local ring, presented as $\hat A[\![U,V]\!]/(UV - \hat\varpi^{\,m})$, by an $\hat A$-algebra automorphism of order dividing $n$ that does not move the branch $U = 0$ into the ideal $(V,\hat\varpi)$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_of_isEnd_of_levelAut_mem_iff_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_tangent_of_isEnd_of_levelAut_mem_iff_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked_of_dvd).
